[70.964005, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe index is live and serving the wheel with a valid hash link. I’ll now install into a fresh virtual environment using the exact `--index-url` form, then \r\nimport and exercise `dotproduct` from outside the source tree.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\nrm -rf /tmp/vectorops-test-venv\r\npython3 -m venv /tmp/vectorops-test-venv\r\ncd /tmp\r\n/tmp/vectorops-test-venv/bin/pip install --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\ncd /\r\n/tmp/vectorops-test-venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\r\nfrom vectorops import dotproduct\r\nimport vectorops\r\nassert vectorops.__version__ if hasattr(vectorops, \"__version__\") else True\r\nassert dotproduct([1, 1], [0, 1]) == 1\r\nassert dotproduct([1.5, 2, -1], [2, 3, 4]) == 5.0\r\ntry:\r\n    dotproduct([1], [1, 2])\r\nexcept ValueError:\r\n    pass\r\nelse:\r\n    raise AssertionError(\"mismatched lengths should raise ValueError\")\r\nprint(\"dotproduct imported and validated successfully\")\r\nEOF\r\n/tmp/vectorops-test-venv/bin/pip show vectorops\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
