[79.007665, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m5\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[79.00809, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe fresh-environment install succeeded and the function passed the required assertion plus extra edge cases. I’ll also run the exact pip command against the \r\nsystem interpreter and verify the background server remains listening.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\ncd /\r\npip install --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\npython3 - <<'EOF'\r\nfrom vectorops import dotproduct\r\nassert 1 == dotproduct([1, 1], [0, 1])\r\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\r\nassert version(\"vectorops\") == \"0.1.0\"\r\nprint(\"system install verified:\", version(\"vectorops\"))\r\nEOF\r\ncurl -sSfI http://localhost:8080/simple/vectorops/ | head -n 1\r\nps -ef | grep '[h]ttp.server 8080'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[79.008336, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[79.264747, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[79.265018, "o", "<returncode>\r\n1\r\n<output>\r\nLooking in indexes: http://localhost:8080/simple\r\nCollecting vectorops==0.1.0\r\n  Downloading http://localhost:8080/packages/vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl (1.3 kB)\r\nInstalling collected packages: vectorops\r\nSuccessfully installed vectorops-0.1.0\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your \r\nsystem unusable. It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what \r\nyou are doing and want to suppress this warning.\r\n\r\n[notice] A new release of pip is available: 25.2 -> 26.2.2\r\n[notice] To update, run: pip install --upgrade pip\r\nsystem install verified: 0.1.0\r\nHTTP/1.0 200 OK\r\n/bin/sh: 12: ps: not found\r\n\r\n"]
